    "resource": "aws_instance.web_host",
    "issue": "Hardcoded AWS credentials in user_data",
    "risk": "Plaintext access keys in instance user data can be retrieved by anyone with access to the instance metadata, console, logs, or state/history, leading to credential compromise and unauthorized access to AWS resources.",
    "remediation": "Remove the hardcoded `export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `export AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, and `export AWS_DEFAULT_REGION` lines from the `user_data` attribute. Attach an IAM role to the instance using an `iam_instance_profile` attribute and manage secrets with AWS Secrets Manager or SSM Parameter Store instead of embedding them in `user_data`."
