    "risk": "Allowing `0.0.0.0/0` access to port 22 exposes the instance to brute-force attacks, credential stuffing, and unauthorized remote access attempts.",
    "remediation": "In the `ingress` block for port 22, replace `cidr_blocks = [\"0.0.0.0/0\"]` with a restricted trusted IP range such as your administrative CIDR, or remove the rule and use AWS Systems Manager Session Manager instead."
  },
  {
    "resource": "aws_security_group.web-node",
    "issue": "Unrestricted all-ports outbound access",
    "risk": "Allowing all outbound traffic to `0.0.0.0/0` can enable data exfiltration and unrestricted communication to malicious external endpoints if the instance is compromised.",
    "remediation": "Restrict the `egress` block by limiting `from_port`, `to_port`, `protocol`, and `cidr_blocks` to only required destinations and ports instead of `protocol = \"-1\"` with `cidr_blocks = [\"0.0.0.0/0\"]`."
  },
  {
